-- title:
--   Taylor–Wiles patching data at p=3, cube-free level
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$ and $p = 3$, and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ which is a semistable model (for every prime $q$ dividing $\Delta_W$ one has $q \nmid c_4(W)$) and whose $p$-torsion Galois module over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is irreducible (nontrivial, with no Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodule other than $0$ and the whole module). Assume given $M_0 \geq 1$ at which $W$ is residually modular mod $p$: a normalised weight-$2$ eigenform on $\Gamma_0(M_0)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ containing $p$ such that for every prime $\ell \nmid M_0$ of good reduction with $\ell \neq p$ the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient is congruent to $a_\ell(W)$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}$; assume further that if $p^2 \mid M_0$ then for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$ the only $p$-torsion point of $W$ fixed by the whole inertia subgroup of $A$ is $0$, and that $q^3 \nmid M_0$ for every prime $q \neq p$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a complete discrete valuation ring which is a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes containing $p$ and every prime dividing $\Delta_W$, and let $N \geq 1$ have all its prime divisors in $S$, with $q^2 \mid N$ and $q^3 \nmid N$ for every $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$, with $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$ in case $p \mid \Delta_W$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$, and $p \nmid N$ in case $p \nmid \Delta_W$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$. Assume the weight-$2$ level-$N$ cusp forms have an integral structure (the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the span of the forms with integral $q$-coefficients is everything), and let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[T_\ell, U_q : \ell, q \notin S]$ of level $N$ and weight $2$ to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$ with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for all primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$. Then there exists a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}'$, a domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field, which is a finite $\mathcal{O}$-algebra along an injective local structure map, such that, writing $\theta'$ for $\theta$ followed by the induced map of residue fields and $T = \mathtt{heckeLocal}\,N\,S\,\mathcal{O}'\,\theta'$ for the localisation of the $\mathcal{O}'$-Hecke algebra at the prime determined by $\theta'$: there is an $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra homomorphism $T \to \mathcal{O}'$, and moreover for every proof $hcard_1$ that $W[p](\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ has cardinality $p^2$, every proof $hker$ that the Galois action on $W[p]$ factors through a finite extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, every ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb{Z}/p \to$ residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$ and every Hecke–Galois representation datum $H$ for $N$, $S$, $\mathcal{O}'$, $\theta'$ with coefficient ring $T$, the following two statements hold. First, if $p \mid \Delta_W$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$, then for every universal deformation datum $D$ of the residual representation $\overline{\rho}_{W,p}$ base changed along $\iota$ for the ordinary condition over $\mathcal{O}'$ at $p$ outside $S$ (cyclotomic determinant, ordinary at $p$, unramified at all primes outside $S$), and every local $\mathcal{O}'$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi : D.R \to T$ such that the base change of $D.\rho$ along $\varphi$ is equivalent to $H.\rho$, there is a nontrivial module $Mx$ over both $D.R$ and $T$ whose two actions agree through $\varphi$, together with some $r \in \mathbb{N}$ and a patching datum [`Algebra.PatchingDatum`](def/Algebra_PatchingDatum.html#L39) $\mathcal{O}'\,p\,r\,D.R\,Mx$, that is, for every $n$ a patching level for the ideal of $\mathcal{O}'[[X_1,\dots,X_r]]$ generated by the $(1+X_j)^{p^n} - 1$. Second, the same conclusion holds, with the flat condition in place of the ordinary condition, when $p \nmid \Delta_W$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$.
--
--   This is the output of the Taylor–Wiles patching construction, in the form used by Wiles and by Diamond, attached to the localised Hecke algebra of weight $2$ and level $N$ at the residual eigenvalue system coming from the $p$-torsion of $W$: it produces, after a finite extension of the coefficient ring, a module over both the relevant universal deformation ring and the localised Hecke algebra carrying patching data in $r$ variables, in the ordinary and the flat case separately. It is the specialisation to $p = 3$ and to cube-free Taylor–Wiles level away from $p$, and it is used in the derivation of the bound on the length of the cotangent module of the Hecke algebra.
